# Spell events for scripts. data/events/events.xml (Player) gets four optional hooks, all called with the player as
# self and the spell as (spellName, spellId, spellGroup, aggressive); spellGroup is SPELLGROUP_NONE/ATTACK/HEALING/
# SUPPORT/SPECIAL (now Lua constants):
#   Player:onSpellCost(spellName, spellId, spellGroup, aggressive, manaCost) -> manaCost[, healthCost]
#       called while the cast is checked; the returned mana is what must be available and what is paid (also added to
#       magic level training), the second value is an extra health cost (never lethal: the player needs more health than
#       it, else "You do not have enough health.")
#   Player:onSpellPreCast(spellName, spellId, spellGroup, aggressive, manaCost, healthCost) -> false cancels the cast
#       (nothing is paid, no cooldown); any other return value lets it go on
#   Player:onSpellCast(spellName, spellId, spellGroup, aggressive, manaCost, healthCost)
#       after the spell ran, its costs were paid and the cooldowns set
#   Player:onSpellCooldown(spellName, spellId, spellGroup, aggressive, cooldownType, cooldown) -> cooldown in ms
#       once per cooldown the cast sets: cooldownType "spell", "group" or "secondary" (group of the spell, second group);
#       0 sets none; not called for players with PlayerFlag_HasNoExhaustion
# Without an enabled event nothing changes. Instant spells and runes are covered (players only). The cooldown
# conditions the spell code set in three places are now set by Spell::addCooldowns. Enable the events with
# server/tools/patch_base_events.py DATA --enable-spell-events (adds the entries disabled and the Lua stubs).
# Apply in the server source root after 0007: patch -p1 < 0008-spell-events.patch, then rebuild.
